    <string name="obd_exp_about_message">The engine control unit does not report a particulate filter fill percentage: it is calculated from the accumulated soot and the regeneration threshold.\n\nThe real threshold for your engine is not known yet (other owners report about 6–7.6 g/L).\n\nA record is made at the moment a regeneration starts, when the unit reports a non-zero regeneration status. The log gets the maximum soot before that moment. A regeneration ends when the status stays 0 for 10 minutes.\n\nA regeneration is marked “completed” (the counter grew, or the engine was switched off within 10 minutes after it ended) or “interrupted” (the engine was switched off during the regeneration, or the counter did not grow within 3 minutes). All completed regenerations take part in the average.\n\nIf the app connected in the middle of a regeneration, nothing is recorded. The data is approximate.</string>

    <!-- Report an error -->
    <string name="obd_report_title">Report an error</string>
    <string name="obd_report_message">The full log will be copied to the clipboard. A GitHub page with a ready-made issue will open: app version, phone model, connection status and the last lines of the log. Device addresses are hidden. Check the text and tap “Submit new issue”; paste the full log into a comment if needed. The “.txt file” button saves the whole log to a file and opens the “Share” menu.</string>
